## Completed

- Created the new repository.
- Created the Codex plugin manifest.
- Created the first skill skeleton.
- Recorded the portable-core and adapter boundary.
- Added verification status and evidence-report contracts.
- Added positive, negative, and unavailable-backend fixtures.
- Documented bounded learning and the human-promotion boundary.
- Added ADR-0002 for the learning architecture.
- Added the bounded-learning specification, TODO, and implementation plan.
- Added the candidate-lesson JSON schema.
- Added the standard-library candidate validator.
- Added six candidate contract tests.
- Added six standalone security and regression fixtures.
- Added prompt-injection detection to candidate validation.
- Added explicit approve, reject, supersede, and revert transitions.
- Added versioned approved/rejected/superseded lesson storage.
- Added the explicitly invoked `savant-learning-review` skill.
- Added six promotion lifecycle tests and four measurement tests; the full
  suite now passes 28 tests.
- Added timezone, evidence-reference, nested-contract, manifest, and
  frontmatter regression coverage.
- Added rollback-safe supersession for partial promotion failures.
- Reconciled architecture, specification, plan, TODO, policy, and status
  language with the implemented pilot boundary.
- Promoted `lesson-proof-001` from the planted proof-error fixture.
- Recorded a baseline versus review-only measurement: 15 vs 78 estimated
  tokens; both paths preserved `FAILED`.
- Confirmed normal verification loads no learning context.

